## 7. Security page

Goal: say only what can be proven, and say it clearly.

| Claim | Source in the app | Publish? |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Items are encrypted in your browser before anything is sent | Import page copy | Yes |
| Cyfer’s server never sees a value read by a connected app | Connected apps copy | Yes, scoped to connected apps |
| Every app read is logged | Connected apps copy | Yes |
| Breach check sends only 5 characters of a hash | Health and Tools copy | Yes |
| No recovery without your keys | Delete account copy | Yes, as an honesty point |
| Sage sees metadata only | Sage page | Yes |
| Website icons load from your browser, not Cyfer’s server | Settings copy | Yes |
| Auto-lock and a per-device unlock key | Settings copy | Yes |
| Passkey sign-in | Getting started | Yes, once confirmed |
| Independent audit, pen test, SOC 2, ISO | None | No until a report exists |
| Reproducible builds | None | No until you confirm what self-hosters receive |
| Open source | Not true | No |

* **Layout:** short promise at the top, the table above rewritten as plain cards, an architecture diagram, a “what we cannot see” panel, a “what happens if you lose your keys” panel, and a downloadable whitepaper (needs your technical details).
* **Interactive:** a diagram where you click “your browser”, “Cyfer server”, “connected app” to see what each can read.
* **Video:** 45-second explainer of the encryption path.

